# Ransack Filtering

**Always use Ransack** for server-side filtering and sorting. No manual `where` chains.

## Controller Pattern

Pass `params[:q]` (already available as `q_params` from `ApplicationController`) to `ransack`:

```ruby
def index
  scope = Post.includes(:author)
              .ransack(q_params)
              .result

  render inertia: "Posts/Index", props: {
    posts: inertia_scroll(scope.order(created_at: :desc)) { |records|
      records.map { |p| PostResource.new(p).to_h }
    },
    filters: q_params,
  }
end
```

**Key points:**
- `q_params` is defined in `ApplicationController` as `params[:q] || {}`
- `ransack(q_params).result` returns an ActiveRecord relation — chain `.order`, `.includes`, etc. after it
- Pass `filters: q_params` back to the frontend so filter controls reflect current state
- Ransack predicates are appended to the field name: `name_cont`, `state_eq`, `created_at_gteq`

## Common Predicates

| Predicate | SQL | Example param |
|-----------|-----|---------------|
| `_eq` | `= value` | `q[state_eq]=active` |
| `_not_eq` | `!= value` | `q[state_not_eq]=archived` |
| `_cont` | `LIKE %value%` | `q[name_cont]=john` |
| `_in` | `IN (values)` | `q[state_in][]=active&q[state_in][]=pending` |
| `_gteq` / `_lteq` | `>=` / `<=` | `q[created_at_gteq]=2024-01-01` |
| `_present` | `IS NOT NULL AND != ''` | `q[email_present]=true` |
| `_null` | `IS NULL` | `q[deleted_at_null]=true` |
| `_start` / `_end` | `LIKE value%` / `LIKE %value` | `q[name_start]=Jo` |

## Frontend — Sending Filters via `router.get`

Filters live in query params under the `q` key. Use `router.get` to update — this triggers a full server round-trip and resets infinite scroll state automatically:

```tsx
const onFilterChange = (key: string, value: string | null) => {
  const q = { ...filters };
  if (value) {
    q[key] = value;
  } else {
    delete q[key];
  }
  router.get(currentUrl, { q }, { preserveState: true, preserveScroll: true });
};
```

For text search with debounce:

```tsx
const onSearch = useDebouncedCallback((value: string) => {
  const q = { ...filters, name_cont: value || undefined };
  router.get(currentUrl, { q }, { preserveState: true, preserveScroll: true });
}, 300);
```

## Model — Allowlisting Searchable Attributes

By default Ransack allows searching all model attributes. Restrict with `ransackable_attributes` and `ransackable_associations`:

```ruby
class Post < ApplicationRecord
  def self.ransackable_attributes(auth_object = nil)
    %w[title state agent_type created_at]
  end

  def self.ransackable_associations(auth_object = nil)
    %w[author project]
  end
end
```

**CRITICAL:** Without `ransackable_attributes`, Ransack raises `UnfilteredParameters` in strict mode or silently allows filtering on any column. Always define it on models exposed to user-controlled params.

## Combining with Pagination

Ransack `.result` returns a relation. Pass it to `inertia_scroll` or `paginate`:

```ruby
scope = Model.ransack(q_params).result
# Inertia infinite scroll
posts: inertia_scroll(scope.order(created_at: :desc)) { |r| r.map { ... } }
# JSON API
pagy, records = paginate(scope.order(created_at: :desc))
```

## Anti-Patterns

```ruby
# ❌ Manual filter chains
scope = scope.where(agent_type: params[:agent]) if params[:agent].present?
scope = scope.where(state: params[:state]) if params[:state].present?

# ✅ Ransack
scope = Model.ransack(q_params).result
# Frontend sends: ?q[agent_type_eq]=claude_code&q[state_eq]=running
```

```ruby
# ❌ Custom sorting logic
scope = scope.order(params[:sort] => params[:direction])

# ✅ Ransack sorts
scope = Model.ransack(q_params.merge(s: "created_at desc")).result
# Or from frontend: ?q[s]=created_at+desc
```
